-> invariant and concurrent-call protection once implemented.
+`CallNextTicket` holds the domain rules; see
+[`business-rules.md`](business-rules.md) ("Call next") for the full list. The
+queue-row lock serializes call and issuance/deactivation on MariaDB. Because
+`Ticket::call()` does not lock the queue, the candidate row is locked and
+re-checked as `waiting` before it is marked called, so a ticket can be called
+only once. The single-call and race-skip behavior is covered by
+`tests/Feature/CallNextTicketTest.php` and `tests/Feature/IssueTicketTest.php`.
+Row-level locking itself is a no-op on SQLite, so the true multi-connection
+race is only exercised by the MariaDB deployment, not by the test suite.
 
