@@ -98,7 +98,21 @@ ### Ticket
 
 **Immutability enforcement:** the write-once rule is enforced on the `Ticket` model (`updating` hook), so it applies to Eloquent saves only — mass updates through the query builder (`Ticket::query()->update(...)`) bypass it and must not be used on issued tickets.
 
-**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields; deterministic call-next selection (priority + age + 3-ticket fairness) and HTTP/Livewire panels remain out of scope per #14.
+**Single-ticket call (scope note):** `Ticket::call()` marks one waiting ticket as `called` (entity-membership checked, exactly-once). This minimal domain primitive proves the mutable `status`/`called_*` fields.
+
+**Call next (implementation):** `App\Actions\CallNextTicket` selects and calls the next ticket of a queue. It is invoked as `(new CallNextTicket)($queue, $calledBy, $mode)` with `App\Enums\CallMode`:
+
+- **Candidates:** only `waiting` tickets of the given queue. Called tickets and tickets of other queues are never candidates.
+- **Ordering:** `priority` descending, then `issued_at` ascending, then `id` ascending. Deterministic for the same state.
+- **`CallMode::Any`:** full ordering, subject to the fairness rule below.
+- **`CallMode::PriorityOnly`:** only tickets with `priority > 0`; fairness is ignored.
+- **`CallMode::NormalOnly`:** only tickets with `priority = 0`; fairness is ignored.
+- **Fairness (Any only):** the last 3 called tickets of the queue (most recent by `called_at`, then `id`, across all modes) are inspected. If there are 3, all are priority, and at least one normal ticket is waiting, only normal tickets are eligible. A normal call resets the streak. If no normal waits, priority tickets keep being called.
+- **Inactive queue:** rejected with `App\Exceptions\InactiveQueueException`; the queue state is read under a row lock inside the transaction, not from the passed instance. Nothing changes.
+- **No eligible ticket** (empty queue, or no priority/normal ticket for the mode): `App\Exceptions\NoWaitingTicketsException`; nothing changes.
+- **Exactly-once:** inside the transaction the queue row is locked, the candidate is picked, then the candidate row is locked and re-checked as `waiting`. If a concurrent `Ticket::call()` (which does not lock the queue) already called it, that candidate is skipped and the next one is picked.
+- **Result:** the winner gets `status = called`, `called_at = now()` and `called_by_user_id`, and the updated model is returned. Only those three fields change (write-once rule still applies).
+- **Authorization:** not performed by the action (out of scope); the caller is trusted. HTTP/Livewire and per-queue permissions are separate work.
 
 ### Priority
 
